cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: Shen
    given-names: Dapeng
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-7836-6225"
title: "MINT: manufactured-null invariant testing for auditing machine-generated financial time series"
version: 1.0.1
date-released: "2026-09-01"
repository-code: "https://github.com/chengzijiang05-tech/mint-audit"
abstract: >-
  Code, frozen experimental results, and figure-generation scripts for
  the paper "Manufactured nulls: orbit-contrastive learning with
  anytime-valid evidence for auditing machine-generated financial series".
  The framework manufactures the null that a machine-generated sequence
  must survive: five surrogate operators with published mechanisms turn
  each reference window into an orbit of forged twins, a contrastive
  encoder learns the separating statistic from real windows alone, and an
  orbit-normalized e-value converts the score gap into evidence that is
  exact by exchangeability and valid under any stopping rule.
keywords:
  - machine-generated time series
  - financial forensics
  - e-values
  - anytime-valid inference
  - contrastive learning
